== B1: any backend failure is journalled as MISSING (immutable) — wrong/expired credentials, 5xx
  the object is intact on disk: True
  scrub with a rejected signature (HTTP 403 for every GET) returned: RAISED ObjectStoreError: GET tnt_demo/sha256/04/0472937c29d331bd6d0b5bfc89ce846b3911299742500082d7cc2e43dc2f4772: HTTP 403 <?xml version='1.0'?><Error><Code>Signatur
  journal: OK
  consequence: observation naming the intact original: accepted
  store.check on a 403: RAISES ObjectStoreError | store.get on a 403 raises: ObjectStoreError GET tnt_demo/sha256/04/0472937c29d331bd6d0b5bfc89ce846b39112

== B2: client signs Host with an explicit default port, the HTTP library sends it without -> every request 403
  signed host: s3.example.com | Host header actually sent by http.client/urllib3: [b'Host: s3.example.com']

== B3: the gateway's database session is a SUPERUSER session (SET SESSION AUTHORIZATION), not role ac_storage
  through gateway._psql: RAISES RuntimeError: ERROR:  permission denied for table source_bytes
  login roles that are members of ac_storage: 1
  scrub(tenant=<payload>) under python3 (default): ValueError недопустимый tenant: 'x$gw$; RESET SESSION AUTHORIZATION; CREATE TABLE IF NOT E | injected table exists: no
  scrub(tenant=<payload>) under python3 -O: ValueError недопустимый tenant: 'x$gw$; RESET SESSION AUTHORIZATION; CREATE TABLE IF NOT E | injected table exists: no

== B4: scrub stamps results at the END of the run (database clock at insert), not when the object was read
  object damaged at 2026-10-02 02:14:30.446479+03 | journal says: OK checked_at=2026-10-02 02:14:33.48878+03 | really now: CORRUPT

== B5: one registry row with an odd tenant stops every later scrub (rows are immutable)
  poisoned row refused at insert: ERROR:  new row for relation "objects" violates check constraint "objects_tenant_id_check"

== B6: tenant isolation by prefix — listing
  FsBackend.keys('tnt_ab') -> ['tnt_ab', 'tnt_abc'] | S3Backend.keys('tnt_ab') -> ['tnt_ab', 'tnt_abc']
  tenant-safe ObjectStore.keys('tnt_ab') -> ['tnt_ab'] / ['tnt_ab']
  object_key accepts tenants the schema forbids (^tnt_[a-z0-9_]{2,64}$): [] (S6R-09 fix: object_key now validates too)
  tenants with '/', '..', upper case, '-', newline, empty: refused by object_key

== B7: SigV4 — independent implementation vs object_store.sigv4_signature
  put object                                     same
  list prefix+token (+/= space)                  same
  query names whose raw and encoded order differ same
  key with space, '+', '%', unicode              same

== B8: what the emulator does NOT check (real S3/MinIO do) — so the suite cannot see these client faults
  region 'zz-nowhere-9' in the credential scope: HTTP 400 (real: 400 AuthorizationHeaderMalformed)
  x-amz-date 20000101T000000Z (26 years old, replay): HTTP 403 (real: 403 RequestTimeTooSkewed)
  GET /originals/../originals2/secret.txt (bucket escape, fpath() compares string prefixes): HTTP 400 b"<?xml version='1.0'?"
  the emulator verifies signatures with the client's own sigv4_signature (s3_emulator.py imports it): a shared canonicalisation fault is invisible
